1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,265
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:05,097
- Oink. Oink.
- What the...

3
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:06,825
GORDON: <i>A cop was
murdered last night.</i>

4
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,431
A bag man on your pay roll?

5
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:10,444
<i>I think someone is trying
to send you a message.</i>

6
00:00:10,944 --> 00:00:11,944
Grenade!

7
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:16,601
- We have unfinished business.
- Listen, if you think you're gonna...

8
00:00:16,817 --> 00:00:19,013
Don't talk about my mother!

9
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,815
BARBARA: An
opportunity awaits you.

10
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,324
SELINA: <i>With you and Barbara,</i>

11
00:00:25,092 --> 00:00:27,994
the three of us could give all
those creeps a run for their money.

12
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:31,327
PENGUIN: <i>She's making alliances
with politicians, building a fortress,</i>

13
00:00:31,965 --> 00:00:33,456
She's been planning a war.

14
00:00:34,468 --> 00:00:36,494
Oswald, I want you
to know I forgive you.

15
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:39,397
- PENGUIN: Just started an orphanage?
- I wanted to surprise you.

16
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:40,873
RA'S: If you don't kill me,

17
00:00:40,974 --> 00:00:44,342
I will kill everyone you love.

18
00:00:45,178 --> 00:00:46,544
(GROANING)

19
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:54,354
It doesn't stop till I've
butchered every single swine

20
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:56,014
on Penguin's payroll.

21
00:00:56,089 --> 00:00:59,457
We both know, Captain
Bullock, you deserve this.

22
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:00,817
Hold on, buddy.

23
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,988
<i>How long have you been
taking money from Penguin?</i>

24
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:05,658
You gotta understand,
Jim, the debts I got...

25
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:06,732
Stops now.

26
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:19,774
Called dibs on my office?

27
00:01:21,782 --> 00:01:24,616
- I ain't dead yet.
- Just measuring for when you are.

28
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:27,780
Shouldn't you be
resting? Lemme help you.

29
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:29,288
I'm fine.

30
00:01:31,592 --> 00:01:32,592
Great.

31
00:01:32,693 --> 00:01:35,128
So we can talk about you
taking Penguin's money.

32
00:01:35,228 --> 00:01:37,720
- I'm not that fine.
- I meant what I said, Harvey.

33
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:40,563
- This stops today, you hear me?
- OFFICER: Hey, hey!

34
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:42,960
What the hell is that?

35
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,380
You're trying to
change the subject.

36
00:01:44,404 --> 00:01:47,272
Obviously. But seriously,
what the hell is that?

37
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:49,307
(GUNS COCKING)

38
00:01:50,811 --> 00:01:51,811
OFFICER: Is that blood?

39
00:02:03,757 --> 00:02:05,953
DELIVERY MAN: Some
fancy-ass guy on the phone.

40
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:08,551
How was I supposed to
know what we were carrying?

41
00:02:08,629 --> 00:02:10,962
Stench of death, for starters.

42
00:02:11,064 --> 00:02:12,430
I got a cold.

43
00:02:12,499 --> 00:02:15,731
Forty-four boxes. One for
every cop in the precinct.

44
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:17,302
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

45
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:19,662
Pyg's escalating.

46
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:21,333
He's not just after
dirty cops anymore,

47
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:22,843
it's the whole GCPD.

48
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:25,336
There are 45 cops here.

49
00:02:25,445 --> 00:02:27,023
DELIVERY MAN: Oh,
yeah. The instructions said,

50
00:02:27,047 --> 00:02:29,778
"Don't give nothing to this
one cop here, named..."

51
00:02:30,884 --> 00:02:32,352
Uh...

52
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:33,653
Jim Gordon?

53
00:02:41,595 --> 00:02:43,115
- (GUESTS CHATTERING)
- (MUSIC PLAYING)

54
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,962
Support are really pleased
that you enjoyed the finger food.

55
00:02:50,137 --> 00:02:51,196
Helping the needy.

56
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:54,130
Very good for the
soul, Master Bruce.

57
00:02:56,243 --> 00:02:58,075
I have to say I
really appreciate you

58
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,698
allowing us to do
the fundraiser here.

59
00:03:01,048 --> 00:03:03,040
The society meant a
great deal to your father.

60
00:03:03,817 --> 00:03:05,615
As long as I don't
have to leave the house.

61
00:03:06,053 --> 00:03:07,612
Well, you're Bruce
Wayne, ain't you?

62
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,650
The world can come to you.

63
00:03:11,892 --> 00:03:13,053
Hey. What the hell?

64
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,628
- Excuse me?
- You knocked into me.

65
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:15,695
Bruce...

66
00:03:16,797 --> 00:03:18,757
- Sorry, I didn't notice...
- Well, you should've.

67
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:20,562
- Bruce...
- Honestly, I'm really sorry.

68
00:03:33,613 --> 00:03:35,104
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

69
00:03:41,088 --> 00:03:42,648
I haven't wanted to
push, Master Bruce.

70
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:47,016
I mean, what happened with Ra's.

71
00:03:48,195 --> 00:03:49,356
I know that you're hurting.

72
00:03:52,299 --> 00:03:54,962
- Just please tell me what I can do...
- You can get off my back!

73
00:03:58,305 --> 00:03:59,305
Sorry.

74
00:04:00,874 --> 00:04:01,874
I just...

75
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,146
I can't stop thinking

76
00:04:08,515 --> 00:04:09,515
about

77
00:04:11,518 --> 00:04:12,518
what I...

78
00:04:18,024 --> 00:04:19,287
I should feel bad,

79
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:22,693
guilty, I...

80
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,290
- I'd just...
- You're just angry.

81
00:04:29,136 --> 00:04:33,096
That anger is concealing
what's really going on.

82
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:36,302
Unless you face it full on,

83
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,943
it will consume you

84
00:04:40,547 --> 00:04:41,547
and it'll erupt.

85
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:47,910
I know what you're capable of.

86
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:52,790
And I don't want to see
you or anybody else get hurt.

87
00:04:57,798 --> 00:04:58,798
I need some air.

88
00:05:09,943 --> 00:05:10,983
GORDON: (SIGHS) All right.

89
00:05:14,181 --> 00:05:17,117
Next time you see red stuff
dripping from a package,

90
00:05:17,184 --> 00:05:20,018
- consider calling the police.
- Where's COD?

91
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:22,320
Get the hell out of here.

92
00:05:23,757 --> 00:05:24,757
Hey, Jim...

93
00:05:29,896 --> 00:05:33,458
James, I am so happy we
are working hand in hand

94
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:35,559
to rid the city of this
menace. (CHUCKLES)

95
00:05:36,203 --> 00:05:38,968
- He just showed up to offer his help.
- Did he?

96
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,968
Nice to meet you,
Jim. I'm Headhunter.

97
00:05:42,876 --> 00:05:44,037
I'm sure you've heard of me.

98
00:05:44,778 --> 00:05:46,770
My new security consultant.

99
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:50,978
Recommended by Victor,
who is off visiting his bubby.

100
00:05:51,051 --> 00:05:52,611
You wanna know
why I carry two pistols?

101
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:53,853
Overcompensation?

102
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,323
See, I always shoot twice.

103
00:05:56,890 --> 00:06:00,327
The first one does the job every
time, but the second one, well,

104
00:06:01,428 --> 00:06:03,192
that's just my signature. Hmm.

105
00:06:03,597 --> 00:06:04,597
He has a signature.

106
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:08,259
- Colorful, isn't he? But effective.
- Mmm.

107
00:06:08,768 --> 00:06:11,829
Mr. Headhunter and my
men will help the GCPD

108
00:06:11,905 --> 00:06:13,874
until this Pyg
situation is resolved.

109
00:06:13,974 --> 00:06:16,739
We don't want your help
or that of your idiot hitman.

110
00:06:18,678 --> 00:06:20,510
Pyg's actions
threaten the both of us.

111
00:06:21,147 --> 00:06:24,879
He's killing my
cops, my employees.

112
00:06:25,485 --> 00:06:26,485
Allegedly.

113
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:28,249
Get this through
you head, Oswald.

114
00:06:28,855 --> 00:06:32,223
We don't work for you, and
we don't work with you, ever.

115
00:06:32,592 --> 00:06:33,753
(LAUGHS)

116
00:06:34,361 --> 00:06:38,128
Well, your captain
says otherwise.

117
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,225
Excited to work with you, Jim.

118
00:06:46,373 --> 00:06:48,417
- Are you out of your freakin' mind?
- Jim, listen...

119
00:06:48,441 --> 00:06:50,000
You are legitimizing
him, Harvey.

120
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:53,672
He's been legitimized for
years, he was the freakin' mayor.

121
00:06:54,381 --> 00:06:55,925
GORDON: Is it about
the money, is that it?

122
00:06:55,949 --> 00:06:56,949
It's not about that.

123
00:06:57,884 --> 00:06:59,011
How can I know that?

124
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:02,446
- How can <i>you</i> even know that?
- Take a look out there, okay?

125
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:03,921
Half the precinct skipped town

126
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:06,391
because they didn't want to
wear bacon flavored death masks.

127
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:07,927
We need the help.

128
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:10,822
You are dangerously
overreacting.

129
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:13,992
I'm overreacting because every
cop in this precinct got a death threat.

130
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,693
Except, of course, for you.

131
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:16,862
So Penguin's guys are gonna

132
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:18,735
beat and torture their
way through the city,

133
00:07:18,805 --> 00:07:20,967
- then execute Pyg if they find him?
- And?

134
00:07:21,908 --> 00:07:23,137
And the people need to know

135
00:07:23,243 --> 00:07:25,144
they don't need gangsters
to keep them safe.

136
00:07:25,712 --> 00:07:28,409
I'll tell you what, I'm
gonna find Pyg, alive.

137
00:07:28,481 --> 00:07:29,881
And I'll bring him to justice.

138
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:30,950
Good for you.

139
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:33,180
Three cops just went missing.

140
00:07:33,653 --> 00:07:34,653
Where?

141
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:37,591
It's gonna be tough.
It's The Narrows.

142
00:07:42,595 --> 00:07:45,087
So that's it. We're
shutting up shop.

143
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,559
So long, farewell. Toodledoo.

144
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,500
- I can't believe this.
- I can.

145
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:53,432
All this was so I could be
Ra's eyes and ears in Gotham.

146
00:07:53,506 --> 00:07:55,441
He was bankrolling
us, and now, he's gone.

147
00:07:55,508 --> 00:07:56,508
So I'm pulling the plug.

148
00:07:58,345 --> 00:07:59,506
Help yourself to whatever.

149
00:08:01,181 --> 00:08:06,017
So, all of this, being partners,
building something together... Lies.

150
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:09,288
A sales pitch. I
couldn't do it alone.

151
00:08:09,356 --> 00:08:11,621
We can still spy on the
jerks who come in here,

152
00:08:11,691 --> 00:08:13,023
and get intel on jobs.

153
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,953
- We can make it work.
- What,

154
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:18,864
and the three of us stay
together, like a plucky little family?

155
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:22,333
Well, how about a little
parting lesson from big sis?

156
00:08:23,103 --> 00:08:25,265
In this life, you're
on your own.

157
00:08:27,374 --> 00:08:28,374
Always.

158
00:08:31,044 --> 00:08:32,205
Ugh!

159
00:08:32,479 --> 00:08:35,574
Bonus lesson: Never
make bellinis from a can.

160
00:08:41,721 --> 00:08:44,213
I followed a buyer from
The Street Demonz.

161
00:08:44,324 --> 00:08:46,054
They have a chop
shop across town

162
00:08:46,159 --> 00:08:47,991
and I saw exactly where
they hide their stash.

163
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,089
Let's hit it. Show
her she's wrong.

164
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,826
We're not gonna rip off one of
Gotham's biggest motorcycle gangs.

165
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:54,900
Why not?

166
00:08:57,170 --> 00:08:58,900
You and I will find
something else.

167
00:09:00,006 --> 00:09:01,167
(SIGHS HEAVILY)

168
00:09:08,415 --> 00:09:10,043
(SIRENS WAILING)

169
00:09:18,658 --> 00:09:20,024
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

170
00:09:23,029 --> 00:09:25,555
Three missing officers.
Patel from our precinct.

171
00:09:25,665 --> 00:09:27,099
Fazoli and Percoff from the 22.

172
00:09:33,773 --> 00:09:35,298
Good Lord, there's
blood all over.

173
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:37,237
He got 'em here.

174
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:41,580
Clear view from dozens of
windows, someone saw it.

175
00:09:41,648 --> 00:09:42,980
They sure did.

176
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:45,109
All right, bring it in
everybody, come on.

177
00:09:48,788 --> 00:09:50,620
This is The Narrows.

178
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:53,784
The poorest of the poor.
The hardest of the hard.

179
00:09:54,327 --> 00:09:57,786
Now I don't need to tell you that
they got a code of silence down here.

180
00:09:57,897 --> 00:10:00,492
Which means we gotta
make 'em more scared of us

181
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,466
than they are of
their own people.

182
00:10:03,169 --> 00:10:05,138
We go floor by floor.

183
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,012
- Airmail.
- (PANICKED SHOUTING)

184
00:10:14,147 --> 00:10:15,376
(CHUCKLES)

185
00:10:16,916 --> 00:10:18,544
Let's get 'em. Move on out!

186
00:10:23,656 --> 00:10:24,988
This is gonna be fun.

187
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,619
- (OFFICERS SHOUTING)
- (MAN GROANING)

188
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,636
Get off of him! Get back!

189
00:10:49,215 --> 00:10:51,309
Hey! Get off of
'em! Get off of 'em!

190
00:10:51,384 --> 00:10:53,148
They're potential
witness, they're not perps.

191
00:10:53,219 --> 00:10:55,620
This is The Narrows, Gordon.
You think there's a difference?

192
00:10:55,688 --> 00:10:57,657
- Step away, Ruseckas.
- HARVEY: Hey, hey, hey!

193
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:01,661
Ruseckas, they need you
upstairs. You two, go, now.

194
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:06,390
(WOMAN SOBBING)

195
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,499
Working out great.

196
00:11:07,567 --> 00:11:10,662
If it gets me my
cop-killer, yeah, it is.

197
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:11,770
Right.

198
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:20,613
(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)

199
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,680
Bruce.

200
00:11:22,382 --> 00:11:23,611
I just wanted to say hi.

201
00:11:26,119 --> 00:11:28,179
I'm Grace. We went
to school together.

202
00:11:29,489 --> 00:11:30,489
Grace Plumdoll.

203
00:11:31,391 --> 00:11:33,553
Yeah. Sorry, I...

204
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:36,728
It's been years, I
didn't recognize you.

205
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,662
- I heard you were homeschooling.
- Yeah.

206
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:41,433
I am...

207
00:11:43,069 --> 00:11:44,069
Why aren't you in school?

208
00:11:46,072 --> 00:11:47,072
Because it's Saturday.

209
00:11:49,509 --> 00:11:51,029
I don't mean to
knock your fundraiser,

210
00:11:51,244 --> 00:11:53,736
but is there any chance
that you're as bored as I am?

211
00:11:57,350 --> 00:11:59,270
- You'd have to be pretty bored.
- (GRACE LAUGHS)

212
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,184
So, do you wanna
maybe go somewhere?

213
00:12:05,024 --> 00:12:06,024
Yeah.

214
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,692
(INDISTINCT CLAMORING)

215
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,120
MALE TENANT: I don't know nothin'!
Come on, man, just leave me alone.

216
00:12:21,174 --> 00:12:22,174
May I?

217
00:12:22,508 --> 00:12:23,908
OFFICER: Hold it right there.

218
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:25,444
Ma'am, please.

219
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,681
I'm Detective Gordon.

220
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:37,756
We didn't see nothin'.

221
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:39,692
But you knew those missing cops

222
00:12:40,293 --> 00:12:41,955
or knew of 'em, right?

223
00:12:44,063 --> 00:12:48,159
Three officers, different
precinct, same patrol car.

224
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:49,268
They were freelancing.

225
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:52,599
I know how it is down here.

226
00:12:53,139 --> 00:12:55,938
Lot of bad stuff happens, half
the time it's the cops doing it.

227
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:59,344
They were running some sort
of protection racket, am I right?

228
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:04,082
You sit over here.

229
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,477
Yeah? It gives you
a pretty good view.

230
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:09,521
So what'd you see?

231
00:13:09,756 --> 00:13:11,486
Please, I need you to leave.

232
00:13:12,492 --> 00:13:14,222
No one's gonna know
you told me anything.

233
00:13:14,294 --> 00:13:15,819
I give you my word.

234
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:23,498
- Can I help?
- Get out of here, now.

235
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:24,764
(OLD MAN COUGHING)

236
00:13:25,571 --> 00:13:26,571
Will do, Jim.

237
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,840
Hey!

238
00:13:32,745 --> 00:13:34,907
This is ridiculous,
we're on the same team.

239
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:40,752
(OLD MAN GASPING)

240
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,289
Get up. Get up, get up, come on.

241
00:13:43,356 --> 00:13:44,356
Come on.

242
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:50,722
The old lady doesn't
talk, the old man gets it.

243
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:53,891
And after that, I go
apartment by apartment

244
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,559
until I get an answer.

245
00:13:56,369 --> 00:13:57,369
Drop it.

246
00:13:58,037 --> 00:13:59,437
- (GUNS COCKING)
- Back at you, Jim.

247
00:14:00,406 --> 00:14:01,533
HARVEY: Whoa!

248
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:03,905
Whoa. Everybody stand down.

249
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:06,479
- I'm giving you three seconds.
- I'm giving you two.

250
00:14:06,746 --> 00:14:09,375
No one is counting.
You drop your weapon.

251
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,386
I'll tell you what I saw.

252
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:19,524
He took them.

253
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:23,362
He was driving a hearse.
I didn't see the plate.

254
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:24,696
That's all right.

255
00:14:26,065 --> 00:14:27,065
We don't need the plate.

256
00:14:27,834 --> 00:14:29,530
Just tell me which
direction was he headed.

257
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:30,635
Down 7th.

258
00:14:31,304 --> 00:14:32,304
Heading west.

259
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,240
Hey, thanks, Jim.

260
00:14:36,309 --> 00:14:38,749
You know, I never really did
the whole good cop/bad cop thing.

261
00:14:39,812 --> 00:14:40,812
It's quite effective.

262
00:14:43,983 --> 00:14:45,645
West on 7th, that's
Hoover Island.

263
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:48,385
It's tiny, there's only a
couple of abandoned buildings.

264
00:14:48,454 --> 00:14:50,582
We can canvass the
whole area in 10 minutes.

265
00:14:50,690 --> 00:14:52,716
- Yeah.
- HEADHUNTER: And the second shot,

266
00:14:52,792 --> 00:14:54,192
well, that's just my signature.

267
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:56,693
I know it doesn't look good.

268
00:14:57,196 --> 00:14:58,789
But no one got hurt too bad.

269
00:14:59,198 --> 00:15:00,943
And we got what we
needed, right? You just...

270
00:15:00,967 --> 00:15:02,799
You gotta trust me on
this one, partner, okay?

271
00:15:03,936 --> 00:15:05,976
People, we're moving out
to Hoover Island right now.

272
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:08,405
Let's move, go! Go.

273
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:10,242
Come on!

274
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:31,022
OFFICER: This is the
last building, let's go.

275
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:42,541
I got two in here!

276
00:15:49,582 --> 00:15:50,914
(OFFICER WHIMPERING)

277
00:15:51,918 --> 00:15:53,819
This man's alive,
call an ambulance.

278
00:15:54,854 --> 00:15:56,345
(PANTING)

279
00:15:57,490 --> 00:15:59,459
- Help me.
- We will. We're here.

280
00:15:59,525 --> 00:16:01,187
Jim. Pyg disappeared.

281
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,956
There's no sign of
the third cop anywhere.

282
00:16:03,029 --> 00:16:04,029
All right. Get some help!

283
00:16:06,098 --> 00:16:07,098
Hold on.

284
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:13,470
Oh, God. It's okay.

285
00:16:13,539 --> 00:16:17,032
<i>As you can see behind me, we
just had a major police operation.</i>

286
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:18,743
<i>A raid of some sort
on this abandoned...</i>

287
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,747
Sophia! Look! Those are my men.

288
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:25,281
And there's that Headhunter
person I was talking about.

289
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:28,686
Kind of a moron,
but he is effective.

290
00:16:28,788 --> 00:16:29,812
<i>Found dead at scene.</i>

291
00:16:29,922 --> 00:16:33,359
<i>Another is in stable condition
and on his way to Gotham General.</i>

292
00:16:33,459 --> 00:16:37,021
(LAUGHS) So, technically,
I saved that cop's life.

293
00:16:38,931 --> 00:16:40,797
Such great PR. (LAUGHS)

294
00:16:42,435 --> 00:16:44,961
<i>GCPD. A number of
what I've been told are...</i>

295
00:16:45,037 --> 00:16:47,700
Excuse me, little person. Scoot.

296
00:16:47,807 --> 00:16:49,708
<i>Of former Mayor, Arkham inmate</i>

297
00:16:49,809 --> 00:16:52,870
<i>and alleged crime
lord, Oswald Cobblepot.</i>

298
00:16:52,979 --> 00:16:55,505
<i>It is unclear why Mr. Cobblepot
is aiding the police.</i>

299
00:16:57,350 --> 00:17:01,515
Is co-opting the police not the
most brilliant idea I've ever had?

300
00:17:01,587 --> 00:17:05,524
It is Pax Penguina taken
to a whole other level.

301
00:17:06,058 --> 00:17:07,185
<i>Back to you, Matt.</i>

302
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:10,695
Hello?

303
00:17:11,597 --> 00:17:12,597
Isn't it?

304
00:17:13,266 --> 00:17:15,929
Oh. You don't need
to know what I think.

305
00:17:16,769 --> 00:17:18,431
Well, now I definitely do.

306
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:21,864
(SIGHS)

307
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,041
Ears.

308
00:17:25,244 --> 00:17:28,214
My father never would've
publicly aligned with the GCPD.

309
00:17:29,081 --> 00:17:31,915
They're incompetent
and unreliable.

310
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:36,922
Eventually they will fail, and
fail big, and you will fail with them.

311
00:17:38,157 --> 00:17:39,157
So,

312
00:17:39,992 --> 00:17:40,992
that's what I think.

313
00:17:43,195 --> 00:17:45,562
- Thank you for your input.
- You're welcome, Oswald.

314
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:52,368
Because you have shown
me, very clearly, what not to do.

315
00:17:52,939 --> 00:17:55,704
In fact, I'm gonna
get more involved.

316
00:17:56,442 --> 00:17:57,569
Personally.

317
00:17:59,145 --> 00:18:01,546
Don't ask for my opinion
if you don't want to hear it.

318
00:18:03,816 --> 00:18:04,875
Okay.

319
00:18:24,136 --> 00:18:25,764
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

320
00:19:06,946 --> 00:19:08,471
(CAR ALARM BLARING)

321
00:19:12,551 --> 00:19:15,282
MAN: Yo! The alarm's
going off, what the hell?

322
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:18,189
Someone broke in?

323
00:19:19,525 --> 00:19:21,016
I was... I was under the car.

324
00:19:22,294 --> 00:19:23,353
The stash is gone.

325
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,163
Guy musta got out.

326
00:19:25,364 --> 00:19:27,162
So, you musta messed
up your only job.

327
00:19:29,435 --> 00:19:30,926
Guess it's time to burn rubber.

328
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,365
(GROANING)

329
00:19:32,605 --> 00:19:34,198
Please. No!

330
00:19:35,207 --> 00:19:36,266
- Get under.
- No!

331
00:19:36,542 --> 00:19:38,170
Go on then, do what he says!

332
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:42,480
No, no, no!

333
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:44,617
(MAN SCREAMING)

334
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:53,291
(SIREN WAILING)

335
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:00,030
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

336
00:20:04,737 --> 00:20:06,000
(SIGHS)

337
00:20:06,072 --> 00:20:07,233
- Yeah?
- HARVEY: <i>Hey.</i>

338
00:20:07,573 --> 00:20:08,836
We scanned the entire area.

339
00:20:08,908 --> 00:20:11,002
Still no sign of
Pyg or Officer Patel.

340
00:20:11,077 --> 00:20:12,875
<i>You get anything off Fazoli?</i>

341
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:14,174
No, not a whole lot.

342
00:20:14,914 --> 00:20:17,247
Wait a minute. He's
coming to. I'll call you back.

343
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,375
Officer Fazoli, it's
okay. It's all right.

344
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:23,515
You're on your way to
Gotham General. You're safe.

345
00:20:23,756 --> 00:20:24,756
I'm Detective Gordon.

346
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:28,619
- Yeah, I know who you are.
- You were taken by The Pyg.

347
00:20:28,728 --> 00:20:30,060
Did you happen to see his face?

348
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:32,558
No, he wore a mask.

349
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,200
The others?

350
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:38,069
Percoff didn't make it.

351
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:39,869
Patel's gone missing.

352
00:20:40,206 --> 00:20:41,206
Do you remember anything?

353
00:20:41,674 --> 00:20:42,674
I don't know, man.

354
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:45,105
He was torturing us for hours.

355
00:20:45,544 --> 00:20:49,106
He was singing nursery
rhymes and talking crazy.

356
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:50,915
Oh, jeez.

357
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,049
I watched him bleed out Percoff.

358
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,586
Did he say anything about Patel?

359
00:20:55,688 --> 00:20:57,281
I don't know, I don't remember.

360
00:20:58,023 --> 00:20:59,457
Look at me, look
what he did to me.

361
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:01,288
All right, all right, all right.

362
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:02,594
Let's take a break.

363
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:09,963
Why is he doing this?

364
00:21:12,571 --> 00:21:13,571
'Cause he's insane.

365
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:15,740
But it's more than that.

366
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:19,342
I guess he just reached
a breaking point.

367
00:21:21,847 --> 00:21:26,182
There's so much rot in
Gotham. All of it. High to low.

368
00:21:29,088 --> 00:21:31,319
Sometimes, even I feel
like breaking, you know?

369
00:21:37,563 --> 00:21:39,225
I was on Penguin's pay.

370
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:43,565
Started off with
small stuff, and...

371
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:47,265
Deliveries, and
payoffs, and then

372
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:50,975
it got bad.

373
00:21:51,443 --> 00:21:52,443
I get it.

374
00:21:53,279 --> 00:21:54,804
I've done bad stuff myself.

375
00:21:58,150 --> 00:21:59,345
For Penguin, even.

376
00:22:02,755 --> 00:22:04,155
But you and I can make it right.

377
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:09,060
Once I get Pyg, I'm gonna
take down The Pax Penguina.

378
00:22:09,395 --> 00:22:12,365
And then I'm gonna go after
the dirty cops, one by one.

379
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:17,895
Now you have a chance to make
right what you've done wrong.

380
00:22:19,138 --> 00:22:20,138
Help me.

381
00:22:24,810 --> 00:22:26,073
Pyg is planning something.

382
00:22:27,413 --> 00:22:28,574
Nearby... He was...

383
00:22:29,148 --> 00:22:31,174
Maybe where he
took Patel and he...

384
00:22:31,483 --> 00:22:33,247
He kept saying something about,

385
00:22:34,553 --> 00:22:39,218
"I'll bring justice to where
there's justice no more."

386
00:22:40,726 --> 00:22:42,854
"Justice." The courthouse?

387
00:22:42,962 --> 00:22:44,828
There ain't no courthouse
in The Narrows.

388
00:22:45,397 --> 00:22:47,127
There's one they
abandoned a few years back.

389
00:22:47,499 --> 00:22:49,024
Pull it over, I'm getting out.

390
00:22:49,134 --> 00:22:50,134
DRIVER: Yes, sir.

391
00:22:51,170 --> 00:22:53,196
- Thank you, Officer Fazoli.
- Hey...

392
00:22:54,673 --> 00:22:56,733
You are one of
the good ones, Jim.

393
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:16,791
Hey, Brant, I ran into an
old friend, Bruce Wayne.

394
00:23:19,265 --> 00:23:21,097
Bruce, this Emma
Hsueh and Tommy Elliot.

395
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,293
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

396
00:23:26,372 --> 00:23:27,916
- You two know each other?
- TOMMY: Oh, yeah.

397
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:30,273
Last time I saw this guy,
he punched me in the face.

398
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,106
- I should go.
- TOMMY: Hey, hold on, bro.

399
00:23:38,450 --> 00:23:39,509
I totally deserved it.

400
00:23:39,585 --> 00:23:41,247
If anything, you
should've hit me harder.

401
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:43,913
So true. He was
such a jerk back then.

402
00:23:46,392 --> 00:23:47,883
- Okay.
- Little heads up

403
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,623
next time you just bring
some random kid to my place...

404
00:23:50,729 --> 00:23:53,699
- Parents' place, Brant.
- He's so jealous.

405
00:23:54,300 --> 00:23:56,132
Brant wanted
Grace all to himself.

406
00:23:57,369 --> 00:24:01,636
Whatever. You want a shot?
Maybe sample some party favorites?

407
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,107
I'm good.

408
00:24:03,309 --> 00:24:05,744
I forgot about this
guy, total animal.

409
00:24:06,412 --> 00:24:07,492
So, what do you do for fun?

410
00:24:09,148 --> 00:24:11,117
I used to walk on
rooftops and fight crime.

411
00:24:12,518 --> 00:24:13,518
Now I'm not so sure.

412
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:18,451
Whoa! You're a bigger dork
than I remember. Just kidding.

413
00:24:18,757 --> 00:24:20,419
Hey, whatever happened

414
00:24:20,659 --> 00:24:24,255
to that creepy old guy,
the butler, is he still butling?

415
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,427
I'm kidding.

416
00:24:30,836 --> 00:24:31,836
It's a joke.

417
00:24:32,538 --> 00:24:34,098
But, seriously, does
he butle with you?

418
00:24:34,173 --> 00:24:35,334
- Bruce!
- Bruce!

419
00:24:35,441 --> 00:24:36,602
- Bruce, stop!
- Bruce, stop!

420
00:24:36,675 --> 00:24:39,076
Stop! Bruce, get off
him! Bruce, get off of him!

421
00:24:39,144 --> 00:24:41,079
- Stop!
- Bruce, get off him!

422
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:42,273
- Stop!
- Let go!

423
00:24:45,751 --> 00:24:47,014
So, does he butle with you?

424
00:24:49,254 --> 00:24:51,294
Brant, didn't you say you
had a hookup at that club?

425
00:24:52,291 --> 00:24:54,851
Yeah. Yeah, this
is lame. Let's go.

426
00:25:00,632 --> 00:25:02,760
Brant's a tool,
but this'll be fun.

427
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:22,211
Hello, there, partner.

428
00:25:22,688 --> 00:25:24,486
- You followed me?
- Didn't have to.

429
00:25:25,391 --> 00:25:27,087
Your Captain told me
where you were headed.

430
00:25:27,226 --> 00:25:28,717
(SIRENS WAILING)

431
00:25:28,827 --> 00:25:31,092
I guess he thought maybe
you needed some help.

432
00:25:49,081 --> 00:25:51,550
Hi, Jim. Thanks
for leading the way.

433
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:53,851
We'll take it from here.

434
00:26:10,769 --> 00:26:13,204
Keep watching me like that
and I'll think you don't trust me.

435
00:26:13,272 --> 00:26:15,298
Just give me my money,
so I can get out of here.

436
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,875
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

437
00:26:20,079 --> 00:26:21,756
- Where are you?
- SELINA: <i>Okay, I don't wanna hear</i>

438
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:22,804
<i>how I'm an idiot.</i>

439
00:26:23,449 --> 00:26:25,145
I'm at the Demonz'
place. It's...

440
00:26:26,318 --> 00:26:28,116
- It's bad.
- What?

441
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:32,080
I'm hiding, but there
are three of 'em.

442
00:26:32,791 --> 00:26:35,556
Strapped. And they
just called backup.

443
00:26:36,462 --> 00:26:37,623
You idiot.

444
00:26:37,729 --> 00:26:39,823
<i>How about you yell at
me after you come get me?</i>

445
00:26:40,332 --> 00:26:41,572
TABITHA: <i>Just wait right there.</i>

446
00:26:42,634 --> 00:26:43,634
Kinda have to.

447
00:26:47,039 --> 00:26:48,803
Selena's at the
Demonz', we gotta get her.

448
00:26:48,907 --> 00:26:50,933
Isn't this what they call
a teachable moment?

449
00:26:51,043 --> 00:26:53,103
Let her claw her way out.

450
00:26:53,212 --> 00:26:55,977
- We owe her.
- That is what her salary was for.

451
00:26:57,249 --> 00:26:59,718
Like, she only went there to
prove that we can make this work,

452
00:27:00,252 --> 00:27:01,618
us running heists together.

453
00:27:01,787 --> 00:27:05,087
Oh. Then she might've
considered not getting caught.

454
00:27:05,424 --> 00:27:08,223
She just wants a purpose.
She wants a home.

455
00:27:09,094 --> 00:27:10,094
Then it sucks for her.

456
00:27:10,596 --> 00:27:12,064
You know, I thought
you'd changed,

457
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:13,975
like, maybe you could
think about somebody

458
00:27:13,999 --> 00:27:16,628
- other than yourself for once.
- Then it sucks for you.

459
00:27:26,845 --> 00:27:27,869
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

460
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:30,677
It was my idea to offer
my consulting services,

461
00:27:30,782 --> 00:27:34,810
and I dare say it has
been a smashing success.

462
00:27:34,887 --> 00:27:37,982
The Pax Penguina
taken to the tactical level.

463
00:27:38,056 --> 00:27:41,493
And now we have reason to believe
that the notorious Pyg is trapped

464
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,119
in the courthouse behind us.

465
00:27:43,562 --> 00:27:47,192
Look, I know it's a bit of a
circus, but there was no way in hell

466
00:27:47,299 --> 00:27:49,144
I was gonna let you go
in there alone, all right?

467
00:27:49,168 --> 00:27:50,445
The Pyg ain't
gonna go down easy.

468
00:27:50,469 --> 00:27:52,631
So I say we let
Penguin's thugs go in first,

469
00:27:52,704 --> 00:27:55,037
let them be the cannon
fodder instead of our guys.

470
00:27:55,140 --> 00:27:58,133
It's win-win. End
of conversation.

471
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,709
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

472
00:28:04,483 --> 00:28:06,281
- Yeah.
- THE PYG: <i>Did you know</i>

473
00:28:06,385 --> 00:28:09,014
<i>I spell my name with a "Y"?</i>

474
00:28:10,455 --> 00:28:13,323
I didn't. You want to meet me
somewhere? We can talk about it.

475
00:28:13,659 --> 00:28:16,288
<i>Please, Jim, I'm not that dumb.</i>

476
00:28:16,995 --> 00:28:19,863
<i>Anyway, P-Y-G.</i>

477
00:28:19,932 --> 00:28:23,198
<i>The "Y" is because
it's short for Pygmalion.</i>

478
00:28:23,268 --> 00:28:26,397
<i>Like, I'm creating a
new, better Gotham.</i>

479
00:28:26,505 --> 00:28:30,067
<i>And I'm creating a new you, Jim.</i>

480
00:28:30,175 --> 00:28:31,768
- Really?
<i>- Yes.</i>

481
00:28:31,877 --> 00:28:33,937
<i>Except, there's a slight hitch.</i>

482
00:28:34,346 --> 00:28:37,839
<i>I can't recreate you
if you are, you know,</i>

483
00:28:38,517 --> 00:28:39,517
<i>dead.</i>

484
00:28:40,185 --> 00:28:44,520
<i>Which you will be
if you go in there.</i>

485
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:50,989
- In where?
<i>- Oh! Don't act dumb.</i>

486
00:28:51,863 --> 00:28:53,729
<i>Only I get to do that.</i>

487
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:57,892
<i>Let them play cops
and robbers, it'll be fun.</i>

488
00:28:58,003 --> 00:28:59,003
<i>But not you.</i>

489
00:28:59,171 --> 00:29:01,265
And why should I believe
anything you have to say?

490
00:29:01,373 --> 00:29:05,174
<i>Because you are one
of the good ones, Jim.</i>

491
00:29:11,350 --> 00:29:13,216
Harper! Call Gotham General.

492
00:29:13,285 --> 00:29:14,925
Find out what the hell
happened to Fazoli.

493
00:29:24,162 --> 00:29:25,323
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

494
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:31,597
Check again. Jones. Brant Jones.

495
00:29:31,670 --> 00:29:32,763
I heard you the first time.

496
00:29:33,405 --> 00:29:34,405
He said we could get in.

497
00:29:35,407 --> 00:29:36,407
Nope.

498
00:29:39,311 --> 00:29:41,678
Stupid bouncer's acting like
he doesn't know who I am.

499
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:45,144
He knows who you
are. He just doesn't care.

500
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:50,089
I don't care how
much money you have.

501
00:29:50,422 --> 00:29:52,391
You are a dork
and a freak, Wayne.

502
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:54,585
- You always were.
- Brant, chill.

503
00:29:58,964 --> 00:30:00,091
Gimme a second, guys.

504
00:30:03,935 --> 00:30:05,130
(INAUDIBLE)

505
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:11,103
- It's your fault for inviting him.
- Shut up, Brant.

506
00:30:12,344 --> 00:30:13,744
Wait, who is Bruce talking to?

507
00:30:15,847 --> 00:30:17,008
(INAUDIBLE)

508
00:30:19,351 --> 00:30:20,351
Let's go, guys.

509
00:30:22,954 --> 00:30:23,954
Not him.

510
00:30:26,124 --> 00:30:27,124
Lemme talk to the owner.

511
00:30:28,293 --> 00:30:29,413
You're standing next to him.

512
00:30:30,529 --> 00:30:31,529
I bought the place.

513
00:30:33,065 --> 00:30:34,658
- You guys in or out?
- In.

514
00:30:52,384 --> 00:30:53,477
Can't find either of them?

515
00:30:53,552 --> 00:30:55,350
No, they're not. They've
no record of Fazoli.

516
00:30:55,454 --> 00:30:56,664
They can't find the ambulance...

517
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:57,688
GORDON: Call it off!

518
00:30:58,156 --> 00:30:59,156
Call off the raid.

519
00:30:59,891 --> 00:31:00,891
Fazoli's dead.

520
00:31:01,393 --> 00:31:03,726
The guy in the ambulance
was The Pyg in disguise.

521
00:31:03,829 --> 00:31:06,025
- What the hell are you talking about?
- Pyg called me.

522
00:31:06,131 --> 00:31:07,190
He warned me off.

523
00:31:07,299 --> 00:31:09,359
He used the same phrase
he used in the ambulance.

524
00:31:09,468 --> 00:31:11,494
He fed us the
clue to get us here.

525
00:31:12,371 --> 00:31:13,371
It has to be a trap.

526
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:17,532
So, the insane serial
killer who hates cops

527
00:31:17,642 --> 00:31:20,635
warned you to save your
life, because why now?

528
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:22,510
Because I'm against dirty cops.

529
00:31:22,581 --> 00:31:24,413
Except, all of the
times you are one.

530
00:31:25,450 --> 00:31:27,715
I'm telling you,
Harvey, call it off.

531
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:29,887
Call it off.

532
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,357
I have another
interpretation, Jim.

533
00:31:32,424 --> 00:31:34,188
The Pyg is not
trying to save you,

534
00:31:34,259 --> 00:31:36,785
he's trying to save
himself by stopping the raid.

535
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:40,559
You are being played, and
not for the first time I might add.

536
00:31:41,233 --> 00:31:44,533
We called Gotham General,
they can't locate Fazoli

537
00:31:44,603 --> 00:31:46,037
or the ambulance.

538
00:31:46,104 --> 00:31:48,596
Jim, it's Gotham General.
It's a madhouse down there.

539
00:31:48,707 --> 00:31:51,302
If I'm correct, The Pyg
isn't even in the courthouse.

540
00:31:51,410 --> 00:31:54,778
I came directly from the ambulance,
there is no way he beat me here.

541
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:58,206
You're wrong.
Pyg is in there, Jim.

542
00:31:58,283 --> 00:31:59,283
He's right.

543
00:31:59,384 --> 00:32:01,853
We got a spotter across
the street that got a visual

544
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,286
on Pyg, in there,

545
00:32:03,388 --> 00:32:06,222
standing next to Patel,
tied to a chair. I swear.

546
00:32:06,291 --> 00:32:09,728
Look, I can't explain it.
All I know is this is a trap.

547
00:32:09,795 --> 00:32:13,232
Now you asked me to trust
you, I am asking you to trust me.

548
00:32:16,701 --> 00:32:20,103
God, so tiresome.
Start the operation.

549
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:23,272
Jim, I'm sorry. I'm with
Penguin on this one.

550
00:32:23,375 --> 00:32:25,469
We gotta think about Patel.

551
00:32:26,278 --> 00:32:27,803
Let's move out, people.

552
00:32:29,314 --> 00:32:30,314
You better pray

553
00:32:30,415 --> 00:32:32,179
I can clean up your
mess on this one, Harvey.

554
00:32:32,284 --> 00:32:33,308
You are out of line, pal!

555
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:35,148
And you are gonna get
our guys slaughtered!

556
00:32:35,253 --> 00:32:37,984
Jim Gordon! I am
ordering you to stand down!

557
00:32:39,257 --> 00:32:42,352
Finally, a good
idea, Harvey. Boys...

558
00:32:42,761 --> 00:32:46,493
We've gone over the game plan,
people. You know what to do, let's go.

559
00:32:58,176 --> 00:32:59,508
When's our guys coming?

560
00:32:59,611 --> 00:33:01,079
How should I know?
You called them.

561
00:33:02,080 --> 00:33:03,309
(CRASHING)

562
00:33:11,923 --> 00:33:13,084
(WHISTLES)

563
00:33:14,759 --> 00:33:17,251
MAN: It's about time.
Come on, this way.

564
00:33:31,910 --> 00:33:34,675
I'll draw their fire. If
you see an opening, run.

565
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:35,746
Screw that.

566
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:37,527
Whatever we're doing,
we're doing together.

567
00:33:40,652 --> 00:33:44,350
Well, I guess now we'll see if I
taught you how to use that whip.

568
00:33:44,422 --> 00:33:46,584
WOMAN: Hello, excuse me?

569
00:33:46,992 --> 00:33:49,052
- You guys order Thai?
- No.

570
00:33:49,327 --> 00:33:50,920
Good, 'cause I don't have any.

571
00:33:56,167 --> 00:33:57,260
(MAN GROANING)

572
00:33:58,737 --> 00:34:00,171
- Nice shooting.
- Obviously.

573
00:34:00,505 --> 00:34:01,505
Gimme my cut.

574
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:05,901
- Barbara...
- I'm sorry.

575
00:34:06,244 --> 00:34:09,408
Did you want a hug? I
just killed five guys for you.

576
00:34:11,316 --> 00:34:12,716
Actually, we did it together.

577
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:17,154
So that's it?

578
00:34:18,523 --> 00:34:20,355
We're just over?

579
00:34:22,227 --> 00:34:23,227
Over?

580
00:34:24,229 --> 00:34:26,721
You think I came
down here for kicks?

581
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:30,158
You're coming back to the nest.

582
00:34:30,402 --> 00:34:32,962
We got a shipment coming
in, and a business to run.

583
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:36,901
Well, come on.

584
00:35:09,808 --> 00:35:11,709
- (MUFFLED SCREAMING)
- Hey!

585
00:35:12,377 --> 00:35:14,107
Got him! Come on.

586
00:35:18,249 --> 00:35:19,249
Harvey.

587
00:35:21,052 --> 00:35:22,213
Damn it!

588
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:25,789
Oh, no.

589
00:35:28,994 --> 00:35:29,994
Patel.

590
00:35:30,462 --> 00:35:31,462
Oh!

591
00:35:31,563 --> 00:35:32,724
Oh, no.

592
00:35:33,465 --> 00:35:34,990
- It's a setup!
- (MACHINE POWERING UP)

593
00:35:55,453 --> 00:35:57,012
HARVEY: The exits are blocked.

594
00:35:59,290 --> 00:36:00,290
That's not our guns.

595
00:36:01,026 --> 00:36:02,026
They're pinned down.

596
00:36:05,196 --> 00:36:06,858
- Get in there.
- Mmm-mmm.

597
00:36:08,633 --> 00:36:09,794
Get in there!

598
00:36:32,123 --> 00:36:33,284
(GROANING)

599
00:36:34,225 --> 00:36:35,318
OFFICER: Headhunter's hit!

600
00:36:36,895 --> 00:36:37,919
Ruseckas!

601
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:39,725
Harper! Get Patel. Now!

602
00:36:44,769 --> 00:36:45,769
Shoot the chain!

603
00:36:47,539 --> 00:36:48,539
HARVEY: Look out!

604
00:36:55,246 --> 00:36:56,246
Come on.

605
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:01,011
(GROANING)

606
00:37:49,634 --> 00:37:53,264
I did not order the cops in
there. I do not have that authority.

607
00:37:53,338 --> 00:37:56,240
I made a suggestion,
it was Captain Bullock...

608
00:37:56,307 --> 00:37:58,486
- FEMALE REPORTER: Gordon! Gordon!
- (REPORTERS CLAMORING)

609
00:37:58,510 --> 00:38:01,480
How did you find the courage to
run in and save all of those people?

610
00:38:04,983 --> 00:38:09,717
If The Pyg is watching, the
GCPD is gonna take you down.

611
00:38:14,259 --> 00:38:17,127
And that was Detective James
Gordon with a very modest...

612
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:20,964
Nice one, Gordon.

613
00:38:21,733 --> 00:38:22,792
Very good, James.

614
00:38:28,173 --> 00:38:29,641
They think Patel's
gonna make it.

615
00:38:32,677 --> 00:38:34,168
Congratulations, Jim.

616
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,339
You're a hero.

617
00:38:37,982 --> 00:38:41,680
And I'm just the
cop who shot a cop.

618
00:38:45,957 --> 00:38:47,448
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

619
00:38:53,565 --> 00:38:54,565
This is Gordon.

620
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:57,801
THE PYG: <i>Wow. You were amazing.</i>

621
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:00,332
Oh, I was right about you.

622
00:39:01,072 --> 00:39:03,871
You are a get-things-done
type, Jim Gordon.

623
00:39:05,210 --> 00:39:08,476
Ah, and those things that
you want to get done, well,

624
00:39:09,414 --> 00:39:11,406
they're the same things I want.

625
00:39:11,516 --> 00:39:13,883
Only if you want to go to
prison for the rest of your life.

626
00:39:14,285 --> 00:39:15,548
Now that's just mean.

627
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:17,621
I'm gonna find you.

628
00:39:18,356 --> 00:39:19,380
Oh...

629
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:20,788
I hope you do.

630
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:25,395
Because I want to thank
you, in the flesh, flesh,

631
00:39:25,830 --> 00:39:27,321
<i>flesh.</i> (SNORTS)

632
00:39:29,133 --> 00:39:31,796
<i>Because what you said
about the rot in Gotham...</i>

633
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:35,234
"High to low," so
concisely phrased.

634
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:38,241
Well, it gave me an idea.

635
00:39:39,010 --> 00:39:44,176
The next step in
my plot, it's a saga.

636
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:47,114
It's an epic.

637
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,018
<i>It's a spectacle.</i>

638
00:39:52,757 --> 00:39:55,454
And you're my
muse, Jimmy Gordon.

639
00:39:56,794 --> 00:39:58,194
I'll see you soon.

640
00:40:04,769 --> 00:40:06,362
(HEADHUNTER GROANING)

641
00:40:11,776 --> 00:40:13,642
Man.

642
00:40:13,745 --> 00:40:15,043
(SIGHS)

643
00:40:15,113 --> 00:40:16,411
Well, I guess Gordon was right.

644
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:19,149
You know, we
should've... (GROANING)

645
00:40:30,228 --> 00:40:31,787
Second one's my signature.

646
00:40:31,896 --> 00:40:33,626
(CONTINUES GROANING)

647
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:49,607
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

648
00:40:49,681 --> 00:40:51,582
Dude, this is awesome.

649
00:40:53,184 --> 00:40:55,483
I always knew there was
another side to you, Bruce Wayne.

650
00:40:56,688 --> 00:40:58,486
I think I'm gonna
try it out for a while.

651
00:41:23,181 --> 00:41:24,444
(LAUGHS)

652
00:41:24,515 --> 00:41:26,313
(DANCE MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

653
00:41:59,083 --> 00:42:00,984
(DANCE MUSIC TURNS MELANCHOLY)

654
00:42:13,264 --> 00:42:16,063
Thanks. That's from all of
us, even if they're not saying it.

655
00:42:16,901 --> 00:42:18,836
Thank you, Detective.
You'd have done the same.

656
00:42:18,903 --> 00:42:20,462
Yeah, but not as well.

657
00:42:20,972 --> 00:42:22,565
We got an unlicensed robbery.

658
00:42:22,673 --> 00:42:24,118
I've got a license.
But like I told you,

659
00:42:24,142 --> 00:42:25,462
I just don't know
where I put it.

660
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:27,303
Oh, wait. It's in my boot.

661
00:42:30,915 --> 00:42:32,383
We ain't accepting
these no more.

662
00:43:36,547 --> 00:43:37,547
English-US-SDH
